>> scene court
Water has been brought from the four seas and five hundred rivers. Vasishtha sets the crown on Rama's head, with Sita beside him.
>> pose vasishtha raise
>> sound bell
>> wait 1
>> pose vasishtha stand
Lakshmana and Bharata stand to either side. Shatrughna holds the white parasol. Hanuman kneels at his feet.
>> pose rama give
Rama gives Sita a necklace of pearls, bright as moonlight. She takes it off, holds it, and looks at Hanuman, and then at her husband.
RAMA: Give it to the one you are most pleased with.
>> play tapSpots \{"hint":"coronation.5","spots":\[\{"who":"hanuman","y":110,"icon":"ornament","cue":"bell","ops":\[\{"do":"pose","who":"sita","pose":"give"\}\]\}\]\}
>> pose sita stand
>> pose rama sit
The three queens are there. Kaikeyi stands with the others. No one in that hall looks at her differently, and Rama bows to her first.
Rama ruled for a long time. In his reign, the poet says, no widow wept, the rains came when they should, and old people did not have to bury the young.
>> wash
>> title Ramayana / Told after Valmiki, with reverence
-> END
